    "result_text": "Done. Tests green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What I addressed\n\n**Documentation incoherence (agreed, fixed).** The finding was right: my `MembershipLevel` javadoc listed \"household size\" as a pre-tenure factor, but `of()` never reads household size, and the sibling `CountHouseholdMembers` edit in the same change states household size *doesn't* affect the level \u2014 a direct contradiction. I dropped \"household size\" from the class javadoc so the only factors named are the ones `of()` actually uses (email presence, unique name) plus tenure.\n\n**`Math.min` reframed as a guard (agreed, applied).** Since the pre-tenure factors top out at exactly 3 today, the clamp can't currently fire. Rather than remove the forward-looking guard, I made the docs honest about it:\n- Class javadoc now says the factors are \"held at or below `PRE_TENURE_MAX` (3) by a guard\" instead of implying multiple factors push past 3.\n- `PRE_TENURE_MAX` field doc now reads \"Guard ceiling \u2026 before the tenure bump.\"\n- Added an inline comment at the clamp: `// guard: pre-tenure factors cannot reach level 4`.\n\nNo logic changed \u2014 the acceptance behaviour (new owner capped at level 3) is intact and the suite still passes.",
