    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic placement is good \u2014 tenure belongs in `MembershipLevel` (the stated single source of truth), the `tenureDays` helper is cohesive and private, and the constants are named and documented sensibly. The one real structural problem is a documentation incoherence:\n\n- **`MembershipLevel` javadoc now claims household size is a pre-tenure factor.** The new class javadoc says: *\"email presence, a unique name and household size can carry an owner no higher than level 3 on its own,\"* and the `PRE_TENURE_MAX` field doc frames the cap in those terms. But `of()` only ever considers `email` and `namesakeCount` \u2014 household size is not an input to this computation at all. Worse, the *same diff* updates `CountHouseholdMembers` to restate that household size \"no longer affects the membership level.\" So the class is now internally contradicted by its sibling that was edited alongside it. Drop \"household size\" from the `MembershipLevel` javadoc so the two files agree and the doc matches the actual factors.\n\nMinor, optional (not blocking on its own):\n- `level = Math.min(level, PRE_TENURE_MAX)` can never clamp today \u2014 the pre-tenure factors (`1 + email + namesake`) top out at exactly 3. It reads as a forward-looking guard, which is defensible, but if you keep it, the javadoc should present it as a guard rather than implying multiple factors currently push past 3.",
